Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello friends,

Poppr version 2.9.0 is now on CRAN and should be built for Windows and MacOS within the next couple of days.

Installation
You can install the new version from the R-universe <https://grunwaldlab.r-universe.dev/> or CRAN <https://cran.r-project.org/package=poppr> via:

options(repos = c(
  grunwaldlab = 'https://grunwaldlab.r-universe.dev',
  CRAN = 'https://cloud.r-project.org')
)
install.packages('poppr')

Note: the R-universe is a new platform and will contain the most up-to-date version of poppr in case the one on CRAN gets bumped off.

What's New?
This version contains a new function called `bruvo.between()` from David Folarian that compares individuals to a reference set.

There are also a couple of important bugfixes to genind2genalex() for SNP data and bitwise.ia() for large sample sizes on Windows.

Full details of the release can be seen here: https://github.com/grunwaldlab/poppr/releases/tag/v.2.9.0

All the best,
Zhian N. Kamvar

